[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Experiment admission, window and RMS contracts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXP-CAPACITY-BOUNDARY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Keep experiment capacities inclusive and independent
STATEMENT: >>>
Experiment validation shall admit256measurements and512assertions independently,
and reject larger respective counts with InvalidInput. IDs and references shall
remain otherwise valid when testing these capacity boundaries.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: experiment_capacities_are_inclusive_and_independently_bounded.
These are bounded specification checks, not circuit or provider executions.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXP-ASSERTION-BOUNDARY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve finite inclusive assertion bounds
STATEMENT: >>>
Equal finite lower and upper assertion bounds shall be admissible. Inverted
bounds or a nonfinite endpoint alone shall return InvalidInput.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: assertion_bounds_allow_equality_but_reject_inversion_and_nonfinite_values.
Other IDs, references and units are kept valid to isolate each defect.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXP-WINDOW-CLIPPING-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Measure only the requested recorded window
STATEMENT: >>>
Minimum, maximum, integral and RMS measurements shall use the requested window
and its interpolated boundaries, without including outside samples. Integral
units shall append seconds; RMS shall retain the original signal unit. Unusable
recordings shall remain explicitly unavailable with indeterminate assertions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: translated_window_operations_ignore_outside_samples_and_keep_units,
64generated translated-window cases, Proptest seed2026111929; and
unusable_recordings_remain_unavailable_and_assertions_indeterminate. Fixtures
are explicitly synthetic recorded data, not claimed simulator output.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXP-RMS-STABILITY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve representable RMS amplitude and piecewise-linear meaning
STATEMENT: >>>
RMS shall retain the existing piecewise-linear interpolant meaning without
unnecessarily squaring physical amplitudes that overflow or underflow. Exactly
constant clipped finite levels shall return their absolute level after data
validation. Zero-duration segments shall contribute no energy. The returned
RMS shall not exceed the largest absolute clipped endpoint.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: large_constant_rms_stays_finite_without_squaring_physical_amplitudes,
tiny_constant_rms_does_not_collapse_to_a_false_zero and
triangular_extreme_rms_matches_the_linear_interpolant. Selected constants include
1e154,maximum finite,1e-200,minimum normal and minimum subnormal values. The
triangle reference is amplitude/sqrt(3), relative fixture bound4e-15, on[1,3].
This is bounded numerical evidence, not correctly rounded/global time-axis or
upstream interpolation qualification. See docs/rms-stability-design.md.
<<<
